#: ../../source/Cookbooks/porousMedia/synthetic2D.rst:70
msgid ""
"This step extract surfaces of pore space from the vti file, and "
"triangulate surfaces of the extracted pore network. Then calculate "
"connectivity of the pore network. All these processes can be performed by"
" python API of ParaView_. The used API are listed in "
":numref:`lst:porous:synthetic2D:vti2vtu`. There are 4 filters are used to"
" convert vti data to vtu data which will be used in the next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Cookbooks/porousMedia/synthetic2D.rst:76
msgid ""
"**Clip**: remove solid (or grains) space and keep pore space. The scalar "
"field **im** in the vti file represent pore and solid space. There are "
"only two values (0 and 1) in the **im** field, 0 denotes solid and 1 "
"denotes pore space. Therefore here set :code:`ClipType` as :code:`Scalar`"
" and set :code:`Value` as a value greater than 0, e.g. 0.5. In addition, "
"if you want to remove pore space and keep solid space, a parameter of "
":code:`InsideOut` has to be set as :code:`1` (see line 23 in "
":numref:`lst:porous:synthetic2D:vti2vtu`), the default value is "
":code:`0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Cookbooks/porousMedia/synthetic2D.rst:77
msgid ""
"**ExtractSurface**: after clipping, the data is still a volume data. "
"Therefore the :code:`ExtractSurface` filter has to be applied to convert "
"volume data to a surface data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Cookbooks/porousMedia/synthetic2D.rst:79
msgid ""
"**Triangulate**: although the pore space surface has been extracted, but "
"the surface cell type is not changed and is still :code:`VTK_PIXEL`. In "
"order to export the pore surfaces to stl or vtu format, the "
":code:`Triangulate` filter has to be applied. Now we can save data as stl"
" file which can be used as input file of meshing, e.g. "
":code:`snappyHexMesh`. However, we need to do more, e.g. get rid of "
"unconnected pore, find and split inlet/outlet patches out, find a point "
"in the pore space. In addition, an optional filter named :code:`Decimate`"
" can also be imposed to make the triangulation mesh coarse if necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Cookbooks/porousMedia/synthetic2D.rst:81
msgid ""
"**Connectivity**: calculate connectivity of the pore network, append a "
"field data named :code:`RegionId` which represent the index of each "
"individual (or unconnected) region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/Cookbooks/porousMedia/synthetic2D.rst:83
msgid ""
"Then we save the data as vtu format. Note that the argument of "
":code:`DataMode` has to be specified explicitly, e.g. "
":code:`DataMode='Binary'`, because the default value of :code:`DataMode` "
"is :code:`Append`, which will cause issue for vtu file reading of meshio_"
" package."
msgstr ""

